.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-wifi
.Nd the Patina desktop's Wi-Fi menu
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the Wi-Fi menu the bar's Wi-Fi icon opens, at the bar's right end.
A switch at the top turns Wi-Fi on and off; below it are the networks in
range, strongest first, with their signal and a padlock on secured ones.
.Pp
A click joins a saved or open network; a new secured one asks for its
password first.
The network you're on offers Disconnect.
Escape, a click elsewhere, or the icon again closes it; running it while
one is open closes that one.
.Pp
It talks to NetworkManager on the system bus, which on Ubuntu lets the
active session change Wi-Fi without a password prompt.
On
.Fx ,
which has no NetworkManager, it drives wpa_supplicant through
.Xr wpa_cli 8
instead.
Without either or a Wi-Fi device, it says so.
